hipbw is a C++ code that mimics the global read/write behaviour or an
idealized FFT.

The code is useful for running rocFFT benchmarks relative to a
roofline based on achievable bandwidth on a particular device.
hipbw-rider uses the fft_params struct from rocFFT; this was done so
that we can easily pass command-line arguments which match the ones
used in rocFFT rider, hipFFT rider, etc.

Compilation and requirements:

hipbw-rider uses boost program options.  You must specify the location
of the rocFFT source tree.

eg:
make ROCFFT_SRC=~/rocFFT

To use the NVIDIA backend, compile with

make ROCFFT_SRC=~/rocFFT RUNTIME=NVIDIA
